   "scheme": "row-wise (default_rng([seed, b]).permutation(n)) when the CV is ungrouped; restricted (block) permutation when CV groups are given: with the same generator, the rows of singleton groups and of groups whose size no other group shares are permuted row-wise among themselves (first draw), then, for each group size s >= 2 shared by >= 2 groups (ascending s; groups in sorted label order), whole groups' y blocks are exchanged by a random permutation of those groups (row order inside a block kept). Only groups of a size shared with another group keep their within-group y structure under the null; a group whose size is unique (e.g. the only 3-member group) has its rows permuted row-wise with the singletons, so its rows can draw y from different groups. Every draw is a permutation of y, so the p-value stays valid.",
